# Diagnosis of §10 P2 (reliability-report / Prometheus cross-check) - why it stays open,
# and what specifically is broken. Collected 2026-09-14.

## 1. There IS a public, intentional, anonymous path to Grafana

task_obs.tf sets on the Grafana task:
  GF_AUTH_ANONYMOUS_ENABLED=true
  GF_AUTH_ANONYMOUS_ORG_ROLE=Viewer
  GF_AUTH_DISABLE_LOGIN_FORM=true
By design, for a public testnet dashboard - confirmed intentional, not a misconfiguration.

$ curl -s https://dashboard.testnet.sundialprotocol.com/api/health
{"database":"ok","version":"12.3.2","commit":"df2547decd50d14defa20ec9ce1c2e2bc9462d72"}

$ curl -s https://dashboard.testnet.sundialprotocol.com/api/datasources
[{"id":1,"uid":"prometheus","orgId":1,"name":"Prometheus","type":"prometheus",
  "access":"proxy","url":"http://localhost:9090","isDefault":true,"readOnly":true}]

## 2. But the datasource proxy fails - Prometheus is unreachable from Grafana's own container

$ curl -s https://dashboard.testnet.sundialprotocol.com/api/datasources/uid/prometheus/health
{"message":"Post \"http://localhost:9090/api/v1/query\": dial tcp 127.0.0.1:9090:
  connect: connection refused - There was an error returned querying the Prometheus API.",
 "status":"ERROR"}

## 3. Prometheus itself is healthy - this is NOT "Prometheus is down"

$ aws ecs describe-services --cluster sundial-node-testnet --services prometheus grafana --region us-west-2
prometheus: desired=1 running=1 pending=0, deployment PRIMARY/COMPLETED
grafana:    desired=1 running=1 pending=0, deployment PRIMARY/COMPLETED

## 4. Root cause: Grafana's datasource URL falls back to the wrong hostname

Prometheus and Grafana are separate ECS *services* (not containers in one task), each
registered in Cloud Map under the private DNS namespace (`aws_service_discovery_service.prometheus`,
name "prometheus", in task_obs.tf). Grafana's container-init script is supposed to resolve
Prometheus's real address via `aws servicediscovery discover-instances` at startup
(task_obs.tf ~line 394-405) and set:
  PROMETHEUS_URL="http://$PROM_IP:$PROM_PORT"
But it falls back to a hardcoded default if that lookup returns nothing:
  PROMETHEUS_URL="$${PROMETHEUS_URL:-http://localhost:9090}"
`localhost:9090` can never work in this topology (Prometheus isn't colocated with Grafana),
so whatever caused the discovery lookup to come back empty at Grafana's last startup left it
permanently pointed at a dead address until the task is redeployed/restarted.

## Conclusion for §10 P2

Not a credentials gap - a live, diagnosed infra bug independent of this report. Even with the
public anonymous Grafana path (which does work for the Grafana API itself), the Prometheus
proxy behind it is broken, and Prometheus has no separate public/ALB route of its own
(alb.tf only host-header-routes api_domain and grafana_domain). P2 cannot be closed from
outside the VPC until this is fixed. New action item: SLA-10 (see report §11).
